## The charter — role separation (scoping §4)

The conflation, named first: monotone and conserved are
DIFFERENT ROLES, and the stack's poetry invites merging
them. Entropy is monotone and is NOT conserved (that is its
whole point — it is produced). Winding and mass are
conserved and are NOT monotone (a keeper does not run one
way; it refuses to run at all). Equilibrium is neither: it
is the state the monotone's run delivers you to. Any
single-object version that lets one quantity play two of
these roles is a fiat, and K-MV-CONFLATE is armed against
it. This pin makes the separation structural: below,
`mvRole` assigns each named quantity exactly one role, and
EQUILIBRIUM IS DELIBERATELY NOT A QUANTITY in the record —
it is a characterized state, not a thing that runs or is
kept.

The composite verdict (§4): the stack is three pins and ONE
honest composite exhibit — not one object. The monotonicity
and equilibrium members are already-landed mathematics
receiving record pins; the vortex member is landed only as
a static keeper, its dynamics the one genuinely unbuilt
piece, priced at MV-2. The honest composite is MV-2's seat
read whole — one ring, three roles, three different
quantities — with MV-1 packaging the same three roles at
the graph seat beside it.

